From: OpenWrt local build <root@localhost>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: bulk: do not log normal probe deferral as error

Clock providers may legitimately be unavailable during an early probe.  The
consumer will be retried, so avoid emitting a kernel error for EPROBE_DEFER.
Other clock lookup failures remain visible.

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-bulk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-bulk.c
@@ -28,8 +28,9 @@ static int __must_check of_clk_bulk_get(
 		clks[i].clk = of_clk_get(np, i);
 		if (IS_ERR(clks[i].clk)) {
 			ret = PTR_ERR(clks[i].clk);
-			pr_err("%pOF: Failed to get clk index: %d ret: %d\n",
-			       np, i, ret);
+			if (ret != -EPROBE_DEFER)
+				pr_err("%pOF: Failed to get clk index: %d ret: %d\n",
+				       np, i, ret);
 			clks[i].clk = NULL;
 			goto err;
 		}
